  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A project to increase the income of Mongolian residents with an advanced business model of travel for the sustainable Mongol Olle Trail in Nalaikh and Bajangjirgu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2018, the Jeju Olle Foundation initiated a Trail Travel program in Mongolia as part of the KOICA Social and Solidarity Economy Program named - Empowering Underprivileged Communities through the Mongolian Olle Ecotourism Platform. This endeavor has yielded significant outcomes, including the establishment of a robust regional business model. The accomplishments of the project encompass augmenting residents income and fostering a sustainable ecotourism landscape. Consequently, the objectives for the future involve stabilizing the existing Trail Travel course, strengthening the branding of the Mongol Olle Trail to advance the business model, and cultivating domestic tourism by diffusing the &apos;Trail Travel&apos; ethos within the local community. These endeavors are aimed at ensuring a sustainable business framework. Through the envisaged model, we aim to undertake a sustainable project (2024-2026) that significantly contributes to enhancing residents income.&#xbabd;&#xace8; &#xd604;&#xc9c0; &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed;&#xc0ac;&#xd68c;&#xc640;&#xc758; &#xc5f0;&#xb300; &#xbc0f; &#xc2e0;&#xb8b0; &#xac15;&#xd654;, &#xd568;&#xaed8;&#xac77;&#xb294; &#xbabd;&#xace8;&#xc62c;&#xb808;&#xc758; &#xc5ec;&#xd589;&#xc0c1;&#xd488; &#xb9df; &#xae30;&#xb150;&#xd488; &#xb9e4;&#xcd9c;&#xc99d;&#xb300;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the objective of increasing the income of residents through the advancement of Mongolia&apos;s sustainable Trail Travel Business Model, the following strategic steps are envisaged (1) Ensuring the stability of the trail travel platform, (2) Improving the sales rates of travel products and souvenirs, (3) Cultivating heightened awareness of ecotourism by improving hygiene and facilities on the Mongolian Olle Trail, and enhancing the operational capacity of local residents, expanding the variety of travel products and souvenirs, while establishing diverse sales channels, Promoting the cultivation of a walking culture in Mongolia and positioning Trail Travel as a proactive response to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
